+/**
+ * Batched pblock generator: several components are placed and routed in one Vivado run.
+ *
+ * On large devices the fixed cost of a Vivado place-and-route run dominates small components
+ * (xczu7ev: ~80 s of placement for a 15-LUT FIFO, ~110 s per run in total). Here the
+ * pblocks of many components (the same shapes and variants as GenerateFastPblocks) are packed
+ * into the generation region without overlap, all components are linked into one
+ * out-of-context design (each cell in its own pblock with CONTAIN_ROUTING), and the design is
+ * placed and routed once. Vivado cannot write a cell with its routing outside DFX, so
+ * RapidWright copies each cell's implementation into the component's own synthesized design
+ * (DesignTools.copyImplementation, internal nets only: port and clock nets stay unrouted as in
+ * GenerateFastPblocks). A second, short Vivado run per batch adds the pblock constraint, the
+ * utilization report and the RapidWright metadata, so the library entries have the same
+ * layout as those of GenerateFastPblocks.
+ *
+ * Output lines: "BATCH_OK <component> <pblock>" for each generated pblock and
+ * "BATCH_FAILED <component>" for components without one (to be built individually).
